# Files that belong to the repo but not in a recipient's copy. `git archive`
# honours export-ignore, and pack.py builds the zip with git archive, so this is
# the one place that decides what a recipient does NOT get.
DISTRIBUTE.md   export-ignore
site/           export-ignore
.gitattributes  export-ignore

# Launchers are committed with the exact bytes their interpreter needs, and marked
# -text so NOTHING re-wraps them: not a clone on another platform, not git archive
# (which pack.py builds the zip with), not a contributor's core.autocrlf.
#
# .bat must be CRLF: cmd.exe implements `goto` by seeking through the file, and
# with LF-only endings that seek lands mid-line, so the jump fails with "cannot
# find the batch label" — Update-Windows.bat's `goto :dirty` is exactly that shape.
# .command must be LF: bash would otherwise read the shebang and every command
# with a trailing \r and report "command not found".
*.bat           -text
*.command       -text
